# The 2-Line Perfect Centering 🎯

Centering an element perfectly in both directions used to be notoriously difficult. With Flexbox, it takes just two lines:

```css_not
.hero-wrapper {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center; /* Center horizontally */
  align-items: center;     /* Center vertically */
  min-height: 100vh;
}
```

Whatever is placed inside `.hero-wrapper` will sit in the dead center of the screen!

# Multi-Line Flex: `flex-wrap` & `gap` 🔄

By default, flex items attempt to squeeze onto a single line. Use `flex-wrap: wrap` to allow items to wrap onto new lines!

```css_not
.card-grid {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 24px; /* Sets 24px spacing between all items both horizontally and vertically! */
}
```

- `gap`: Eliminates the need for hacky child margins!
- `row-gap` and `column-gap` can set horizontal and vertical spacing independently.

# Flex Items: `flex-grow`, `flex-shrink`, `flex-basis` 📏

Control how individual child items expand and contract:

1. **`flex-grow`**: Factor determining how much remaining free space the item takes up (default: 0).
2. **`flex-shrink`**: Factor determining how much the item shrinks when space is constrained (default: 1).
3. **`flex-basis`**: Initial default size before remaining space is distributed (e.g. `200px` or `auto`).

```css_not
/* The Shorthand: flex: [grow] [shrink] [basis] */
.sidebar {
  flex: 0 0 250px; /* Never grow, never shrink, stay fixed at 250px */
}

.content {
  flex: 1 1 auto;  /* Grow and shrink dynamically to fill all remaining space! */
}
```

# The Fractional Unit (`fr`) & `repeat()` 🍰

The `fr` unit represents a fraction of the remaining free space in the grid container:

```css_not
.layout {
  display: grid;
  /* Sidebar takes 1 fraction, main content takes 3 fractions */
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 3fr;
}
```

## The `repeat()` Function:
Avoid repeating identical column declarations:
```css_not
/* Creates 12 equal columns */
grid-template-columns: repeat(12, 1fr);

/* 4 columns of 200px */
grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 200px);
```

# Responsive Grids Without Media Queries 🚀

You can build fully responsive grids that adapt to any screen size without writing a single media query:

```css_not
.responsive-gallery {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
  gap: 16px;
}
```

## How It Works:
- `minmax(250px, 1fr)`: Each card must be at least 250px wide, but can stretch up to 1fr.
- `auto-fit`: The browser calculates how many 250px columns fit on screen. If 3 fit, it creates 3 columns; if 1 fits on a phone, it automatically collapses into 1 column!

# Positioning Items by Grid Lines 📏

Grid tracks are separated by numbered grid lines starting at index `1`.

```css_not
.featured-article {
  /* Spans from column line 1 to column line 3 */
  grid-column: 1 / 3;

  /* Spans down 2 rows */
  grid-row: 1 / span 2;
}
```

```
Line 1        Line 2        Line 3        Line 4
  │             │             │             │
  ├─── Col 1 ───┼─── Col 2 ───┼─── Col 3 ───┤
```

You can also use negative line numbers: `grid-column: 1 / -1;` spans across the entire grid from first to last line!

# Visual Layouts: `grid-template-areas` 🧩

CSS Grid allows you to lay out pages visually using named areas like an ASCII diagram!

```html_not
<div class="site-layout">
  <header>Header</header>
  <nav>Nav</nav>
  <main>Main Content</main>
  <footer>Footer</footer>
</div>
```

```css_not
.site-layout {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
  grid-template-rows: auto 1fr auto;
  grid-template-areas:
    "header  header"
    "sidebar content"
    "footer  footer";
  min-height: 100vh;
}

header { grid-area: header; }
nav    { grid-area: sidebar; }
main   { grid-area: content; }
footer { grid-area: footer; }
```

# Combining Flexbox and Grid in Real Projects 🏗️

```html_not
<div class="dashboard-grid">
  <article class="metric-card">
    <div class="card-header">
      <h3>Active Users</h3>
      <span class="badge">+12%</span>
    </div>
    <p class="value">24,591</p>
  </article>
</div>
```

```css_not
/* Macro 2D Layout with Grid */
.dashboard-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
  gap: 20px;
}

/* Micro 1D Alignment with Flexbox inside each Card */
.card-header {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-items: center;
}
```
